        <enumvalue id="struct_a_g_remap_core_1_1_g_i_m_i_merge_fixer_config_1a722cb6b00d05d8e6804e597fc6a16daca6b9d0d690dd35849b77d2c234ce90d90" prot="public">
          <name>NormalMap</name>
          <briefdescription>
          </briefdescription>
          <detaileddescription>
<para><verbatim>embed:rst 
``ps-t0`` normal map, ``ps-t1`` diffuse, ``ps-t2`` light map, under ``ORFix`` -- the
layout a GI 6.x skin&apos;s slots already use, so a source slot on it passes through with no
register moved, and one on the plain layout is shifted UP (with no normal map of its
own, the draw reads whatever ``ps-t0`` holds) :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;` :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;`

Eg. CitlaliWhisperofStars -&gt; Citlali: both sides read the normal-map layout, and the
plain handling would drop every normal map the skin&apos;s mods carry, then issue ``NNFix``
on a shader that wants ``ORFix``
</verbatim> </para>
          </detaileddescription>
        </enumvalue>
