        <name>faceReg</name>
        <qualifiedname>AGRemapCore::GIMIMergeFixerConfig::faceReg</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><verbatim>embed:rst 
The register the target binds its face diffuse to, or empty to leave the face graph alone
:raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;` :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;`

GI 6.x swapped the face&apos;s diffuse and light map, so the diffuse is bound at ``ps-t1`` on the
main pass -- but a MOD may still write the pre-6.x ``ps-t0``, and passing that through
replaces the target&apos;s face LIGHT MAP with it. Normalising is a no-op when the mod already
agrees
</verbatim> </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="include/AGRemapCore/data/IniFixData/GIMIMergeFixer.h" line="333" column="21" bodyfile="include/AGRemapCore/data/IniFixData/GIMIMergeFixer.h" bodystart="333" bodyend="-1"/>
      </memberdef>
      <memberdef kind="variable" id="struct_a_g_remap_core_1_1_g_i_m_i_merge_fixer_config_1a66d058b6d4b21463e1a0b21e2fbbf179" prot="public" static="no" mutable="no">
        <type>bool</type>
        <definition>bool AGRemapCore::GIMIMergeFixerConfig::faceOnlyWhenMoved</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>faceOnlyWhenMoved</name>
        <qualifiedname>AGRemapCore::GIMIMergeFixerConfig::faceOnlyWhenMoved</qualifiedname>
        <initializer>= false</initializer>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><verbatim>embed:rst 
Whether the mod&apos;s face section is copied onto the target ONLY when its diffuse has to move onto
\ref faceReg -- the mod binds it at the other register :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;` :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;`

For two skins of one character that draw the SAME face meshes with the SAME face diffuse hash
(Yaoyao and YaoyaoBamboo: ``c70ae897``), the mod&apos;s own section already fires on the target, and a
copy is a second ``TextureOverride`` section on that hash -- 3DMigoto reports it as a mod conflict on every
reload. A binding by ``this =`` names no register and never moves. The forward direction&apos;s rule
is ``GIMIComponentFixerConfig::faceSwapOnlyFromDiffuseReg``. **Default**: ``false``, always copied
</verbatim> </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
